    "details" : {
      "en" : {
        "id" : "en",
        "purpose" : "To calculate the National Institutes of Health Stroke Scale (NIHSS) total score from the recorded item scores in a structured neurological stroke examination. The NIHSS is a standardized tool used to quantify stroke-related neurological deficit severity, with total scores ranging from 0 to 42.",
        "keywords" : [
          "national",
          "institute",
          "health",
          "NIH",
          "stroke",
          "scale",
          "NIHSS",
          "consciousness"
        ],
        "use" : "Use to measure and assess the neurological severity of a stroke. \n\nIt consists of fifteen parameters obtained through clinical neurological assessment:\n\n- 1a) Level of consciousness (LOC) responsiveness (0-3p)\n- 1b) Level of consciousness questions (0-2p)\n- 1c) Level of conciousness commands (0-2p)\n- 2) Horizontal eye movement (0-2p)\n- 3) Visual (0-3p)\n- 4) Facial palsy (0-3p)\n- 5a) Left arm motor (0-4p)\n- 5b) Right arm motor (0-4p)\n- 6a) Left leg motor (0-4p)\n- 6b) Right leg motor (0-4p)\n- 7) Limb ataxia (0-2p)\n- 8) Sensory (0-2p)\n- 9) Best language (0-3p)\n- 10) Dysarthria (0-2p)\n- 11) Extinction/Inattention (0-2p)\n\nThe maximum score is 42p. Increasing NIHSS scores are consistent with severe neurological impairment.",
        "misuse" : "Not to be used for:\n- Diagnosing stroke or ruling stroke in or out.\n- Producing a score when one or more NIHSS items are missing, uncertain, or not properly assessed.",
        "copyright" : "© Cambio CDS"
      }
    },
    "other_details" : {
      "references" : "Lyden P, Brott T, Tilley B, Welch KM, Mascha EJ, Levine S, Haley EC, Grotta J, Marler J. Improved reliability of the NIH Stroke Scale using video training. NINDS TPA Stroke Study Group. Stroke. 1994 Nov;25(11):2220-6. doi: 10.1161/01.str.25.11.2220. PMID: 7974549.\n\nAppelros P, Terént A. Characteristics of the National Institute of Health Stroke Scale: results from a population-based stroke cohort at baseline and after one year. Cerebrovasc Dis. 2004;17(1):21-7. doi: 10.1159/000073894. Epub 2003 Oct 3. PMID: 14530634.",
      "en" : "The National Institutes of Health Stroke Scale (NIHSS) is an evaluation tool used to measure and assess the neurological severity of a stroke. It consists of fifteen parameters obtained through clinical neurological assessment."
    }
  },
